Cell["\<\
A side is a shortest path from a corner to the next, returned as a directed \
path graph. Polygons on the same corners in a different cyclic order are \
different polygons.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c518f067-4942-41dc-aa15-c6d05c464e70"],

Cell["\<\
In the plane the side fixes a regular polygon up to motion. On a graph it \
does not: on the square grid the squares of side 2 are the axis squares of \
side 2, with diagonals 4, and the diamonds, the four neighbours of a vertex, \
with all six distances 2. Their corners can be taken in any order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e23c8f4b-f312-424b-b07e-6c46d6bc0539"],

